    "updated_at": "2025-08-18T14:23:46Z",
    "body": "The handling of discusion about removing XSLT while hiding the comments pointing that:\r\na) XSLT is now as version 3.0, nearly 4.0\r\nb) The implementation of XSLT in browser can be updated instead of being removed\r\nc) XSLT could look like a niche technology but fill it niche use very well\r\nd) Google, a multi-billions ADS company is *once again* profiting from a open-source developer for free then blame him when he his slow to update his code\r\ne) Google is trying to kill XSLT and RSS for more than a decade now\r\nf) Open this discussion in the middle of the summer and abruptly close it because \"too heated\"\r\n\r\nAre the proof that the decision of dropping XSLT was already made and that #11523 was just a PR stunt.\r\n\r\nIn consequence, Google AND Googlers should be marked as \"bad faith actors\" and should not being allowed to do ANY proposal about the future of the web.\r\n\r\nWe didn't forgot your decade of fuckeries, Google.\r\n\r\nYou wanted some heated comment? You are served.",
